Load the guest window's base from the thread, not from the code (FEX 3bec2ac, on top of 0013)

FillStaticRegs reloads REG_GUEST_BASE (x19) on every JIT entry and after
every call out of a block, and it did so with a constant: the base of
the guest window of the process that compiled the code. Code from an
AOT code cache or the static dispatcher was compiled by the offline
compiler, whose window sits at a different host address than the one
in the process that runs it. Once system call blocks came from the
caches (0013), the first block after a system call put the compiler's
base in x19 and the next guest memory access faulted.

The base now lives in the thread's JITPointers (Pointers.GuestBase,
set in InitThreadPointers) and LoadGuestBaseReg loads it with one ldr
from the state frame, so cached code runs with any process's window.

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/ArchHelpers/Arm64Emitter.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/ArchHelpers/Arm64Emitter.cpp
index 58bdcfa..2ffb7e2 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/ArchHelpers/Arm64Emitter.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/ArchHelpers/Arm64Emitter.cpp
@@ -456,14 +456,15 @@ Arm64Emitter::Arm64Emitter(FEXCore::Context::ContextImpl* ctx, void* EmissionPtr
 #ifdef FEX_GUEST_WINDOW
 // Materialise REG_GUEST_BASE. Called from FillStaticRegs, which every JIT entry and re-entry path
 // goes through, including the ones that resume from a CONTEXT that may predate the register being
-// set up. x19 is callee-saved, so this is redundant after an ordinary host call; a 4GiB-aligned
-// window encodes as a single movz.
+// set up. x19 is callee-saved, so this is redundant after an ordinary host call.
+// WinPad: loaded from the thread's JITPointers rather than encoded in the code, so that code
+// compiled ahead of time (AOT caches, the static dispatcher) runs with any process's window.
 void Arm64Emitter::LoadGuestBaseReg() {
   if (!GuestBase) {
     return;
   }
 
-  LoadConstant(ARMEmitter::Size::i64Bit, REG_GUEST_BASE.R(), GuestBase);
+  ldr(REG_GUEST_BASE, STATE.R(), offsetof(FEXCore::Core::CpuStateFrame, Pointers.GuestBase));
 }
 #endif
 
diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Dispatcher/Dispatcher.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Dispatcher/Dispatcher.cpp
index c81cc60..e8cc73a 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Dispatcher/Dispatcher.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Dispatcher/Dispatcher.cpp
@@ -2952,6 +2952,7 @@ void Dispatcher::InitThreadPointers(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState* Thread)
 #ifdef FEX_IOS_HOST
     Ptrs.DispatcherCbEntryLog = reinterpret_cast<uint64_t>(&IosCbEntryLog[0]);
 #endif
+    Ptrs.GuestBase = CTX->Config.GuestBase;
 
     // Fill in the fallback handlers
     InterpreterOps::FillFallbackIndexPointers(Ptrs.FallbackHandlerPointers, &ABIPointers[0]);
